   "notes": "Described Primer-EZ, the paper's recommended starting point ('a Transformer with just these two easy modifications': squared ReLU + MDHA). The base Transformer's norm type, norm placement, eps, head count, vocab, biases and tying are not stated (they come from the host codebase defaults), so they are not_stated. The layernorm nodes are placeholders and their type is not stated. Full Primer additionally uses: shared Q/K (Q=KW), which was dropped for one-shot runs; normalization after the FFN instead of before it; and a custom layernorm using x(x-mu) instead of (x-mu)^2. The 12X bottleneck and post-softmax gating are excluded by the paper itself. Configs are the T5 settings in which Primer/Primer-EZ were trained. The 1.9B dims (2048/12288/24) are stated only for the baseline Transformer, so they are omitted."
